"<template>\n  <v-stepper v-model=\"stepper\" class=\"elevation-0\">\n    <v-stepper-header class=\"elevation-0\">\n      <v-stepper-step :complete=\"stepper > 1\" step=\"1\">Download app</v-stepper-step>\n\n      <v-divider></v-divider>\n\n      <v-stepper-step :complete=\"stepper > 2\" step=\"2\">Scan QR-code</v-stepper-step>\n\n      <v-divider></v-divider>\n\n      <v-stepper-step :complete=\"stepper > 3\" step=\"3\">Backup your code</v-stepper-step>\n\n      <v-divider></v-divider>\n\n      <v-stepper-step :complete=\"stepper > 4\" step=\"4\">Verify</v-stepper-step>\n\n      <v-divider></v-divider>\n\n      <v-stepper-step step=\"5\">Done!</v-stepper-step>\n    </v-stepper-header>\n\n    <v-stepper-items>\n      <v-stepper-content step=\"1\">\n        <p>\n          Enable 2-factor authentication to increase your account's security. Download a\n          compatible 2-factor authenticator app on your smartphone and click the button\n          below to begin.\n        </p>\n        <div>\n          <a\n            href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.google.android.apps.authenticator2&hl=en&pcampaignid=MKT-Other-global-all-co-prtnr-py-PartBadge-Mar2515-1\"\n            style=\"display: inline-block;\"\n          >\n            <img\n              alt=\"Get it on Google Play\"\n              src=\"https://play.google.com/intl/en_us/badges/images/generic/en_badge_web_generic.png\"\n              width=\"150px\"\n              style=\"margin-left: -10px;\"\n            >\n          </a>\n          <a\n            href=\"https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/google-authenticator/id388497605?mt=8\"\n            style=\"display:inline-block;overflow:hidden;background:url(https://linkmaker.itunes.apple.com/en-us/badge-lrg.svg?releaseDate=2010-09-20&kind=iossoftware&bubble=apple_music) no-repeat;width:135px;height:48px;\"\n          ></a>\n        </div>\n\n        <v-btn color=\"primary\" @click=\"requestSecret\" :disabled=\"loading\" class=\"ml-0\">Continue</v-btn>\n      </v-stepper-content>\n\n      <v-stepper-content step=\"2\">\n        <div class=\"text-xs-center pa-3 mb-5 grey lighten-4\">\n          <img :src=\"qrCode\" class=\"mb-3\" style=\"width: 100%; max-width: 280px;\">\n          <br>\n          <p class=\"body-2\">Scan this QR code with your authenticator app.</p>\n        </div>\n        <p>If you are unable to scan the QR-code, please enter this code manually:</p>\n        <p class=\"grey lighten-4 pa-3 body-2\">{{ secret }}</p>\n\n        <v-btn color=\"primary\" @click=\"stepper = 3\" class=\"ml-0\">I have scanned the QR-code</v-btn>\n        <v-btn flat @click=\"stepper = 1\">Back</v-btn>\n      </v-stepper-content>\n\n      <v-stepper-content step=\"3\">\n        <p class=\"grey lighten-4 pa-3 body-2\">{{ secret }}</p>\n\n        <p>Please write down the secret somewhere safe, you need it in case you lose your phone.</p>\n\n        <p class=\"red--text body-2\">\n          If you lose your phone and 2-factor secret you need to contact support.\n          Restoring access\n          to your account can take some time.\n        </p>\n\n        <v-btn color=\"primary\" @click=\"stepper = 4\" class=\"ml-0\">I have written down the secret</v-btn>\n        <v-btn flat @click=\"stepper = 2\">Back</v-btn>\n      </v-stepper-content>\n\n      <v-stepper-content step=\"4\">\n        <p>\n          To verify that you did everything right please enter your password and,\n          using the authenticator app, a valid 2-factor code below.\n        </p>\n\n        <div>\n          <v-text-field\n            v-model=\"verifyForm.password\"\n            :append-icon=\"verifyForm.passwordShow ? 'visibility_off' : 'visibility'\"\n            :type=\"verifyForm.passwordShow ? 'text' : 'password'\"\n            name=\"verifyFormPassword\"\n            label=\"Password *\"\n            @click:append=\"verifyForm.passwordShow = !verifyForm.passwordShow\"\n          ></v-text-field>\n          <v-text-field v-model=\"verifyForm.code\" name=\"verifyFormCode\" label=\"2-fa code *\"></v-text-field>\n        </div>\n\n        <v-btn color=\"primary\" @click=\"verify\" :disabled=\"loading\" class=\"ml-0\">Verify</v-btn>\n        <v-btn flat @click=\"stepper = 1\">Back to start</v-btn>\n      </v-stepper-content>\n\n      <v-stepper-content step=\"5\">\n        <p>\n          <v-icon class=\"mr-3\">fa-check</v-icon>Alright, your account is now extra secure. Keep your secret safe in case you lose your phone!\n        </p>\n      </v-stepper-content>\n    </v-stepper-items>\n  </v-stepper>\n</template>\n\n\n<script>\nimport axios from \"axios\"\nimport swal from \"sweetalert2\"\nimport { bugsnagClient } from \"~/plugins\"\n\nexport default {\n  name: \"TwoFactorEnable\",\n  data: function() {\n    return {\n      loading: false,\n      stepper: 0,\n      qrCode: null,\n      secret: null,\n      verifyForm: {\n        password: null,\n        passwordShow: false,\n        code: null\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  methods: {\n    requestSecret: async function() {\n      this.loading = true\n\n      const { data } = await axios.post(\"api/v1/two-factor/enable\")\n\n      this.qrCode = data.qr_code\n      this.secret = data.secret\n\n      this.loading = false\n      this.stepper = 2\n    },\n    verify: async function() {\n      this.loading = true\n\n      // validate form\n\n      // enable\n      try {\n        const { data } = await axios.post(\"api/v1/two-factor/verify\", {\n          password: this.verifyForm.password,\n          \"2fa_code\": this.verifyForm.code\n        })\n\n        this.loading = false\n        this.stepper = 5\n      } catch (error) {\n        this.verifyForm.password = null\n        this.verifyForm.code = null\n\n        await swal({\n          title: \"2fa not enabled\",\n          text: \"Unable to verify, please retry\",\n          type: \"error\"\n        })\n\n        this.loading = false\n        return false\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n</script>\n\n\n// WEBPACK FOOTER //\n// resources/js/components/settings/TwoFactorEnable.vue","/*\n Highcharts JS v7.2.1 (2019-10-31)\n\n Boost module\n\n (c) 2010-2019 Highsoft AS\n Author: Torstein Honsi\n\n License: www.highcharts.com/license\n\n This is a Highcharts module that draws long data series on a canvas in order\n to increase performance of the initial load time and tooltip responsiveness.\n\n Compatible with WebGL compatible browsers (not IE < 11).\n\n If this module is taken in as part of the core\n - All the loading logic should be merged with core. Update styles in the\n   core.\n - Most of the method wraps should probably be added directly in parent\n   methods.\n\n Notes for boost mode\n - Area lines are not drawn\n - Lines are not drawn on scatter charts\n - Zones and negativeColor don't work\n - Dash styles are not rendered on lines.\n - Columns are always one pixel wide. Don't set the threshold too low.\n - Disable animations\n - Marker shapes are not supported: markers will always be circles\n\n Optimizing tips for users\n - Set extremes (min, max) explicitly on the axes in order for Highcharts to\n   avoid computing extremes.\n - Set enableMouseTracking to false on the series to improve total rendering\n      time.\n - The default threshold is set based on one series. If you have multiple,\n   dense series, the combined number of points drawn gets higher, and you may\n   want to set the threshold lower in order to use optimizations.\n - If drawing large scatter charts, it's beneficial to set the marker radius\n   to a value less than 1. This is to add additional spacing to make the chart\n   more readable.\n - If the value increments on both the X and Y axis aren't small, consider\n   setting useGPUTranslations to true on the boost settings object. If you do\n   this and the increments are small (e.g. datetime axis with small time\n   increments) it may cause rendering issues due to floating point rounding\n   errors, so your millage may vary.\n\n Settings\n    There